==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Finno-Ugric|śuri-|to die|lang=fi}}, cognate with eg. Estonian {{term|surema||to die|lang=et}}. Compare also {{term|surma|lang=fi}}. The modern meaning is by contamination from {{term|surkea|lang=fi}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|sur|ra}}
* {{rhymes|lang=fi|urːɑ}}
* {{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈsurːɑˣ]}}

===Verb===
{{head|fi|verb}}

# {{intransitive|lang=fi}} To [[mourn]], [[grieve]] (''very often because of sb's death'').
# {{transitive|lang=fi}} To [[mourn]], [[grieve]] (over sb = ''[[partitive]]; over a dead person'').

====Conjugation====
{{fi-conj-tulla|su||||r}}

====Antonyms====
* [[iloita]]

====Derived terms====
* nouns: [[surija]], [[suru]]
* verbs: ''causative'' [[surettaa]]

====Related terms====
* [[surma]]

